OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-$-%%%-!-%%%" ,%-$ -$%%-% ,,
OL,3,GNEWSAHackney voters show Labour's
OL,4,ALondon challenge
OL,5,
OL,6,FMarket trader Les said he neither cared
OL,7,Fabout the party conference, nor did he
OL,8,Fvote. The greengrocer, who has been
OL,9,Ftrading at Ridley Road for 45 years,
OL,10,Fsaid that food prices had become
OL,11,F"expensive", adding: "But we've got to
OL,12,Fget on with it. That's life."
OL,14,FOthers in the market said they were
OL,15,Fworried about the cost of living in the
OL,16,Fcoming months, including the price of
OL,17,Fenergy, food and rent.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
